<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Macquarie Harbour</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Macquarie Harbour is a large, shallow inlet on the remote west coast of Tasmania, entered through a narrow passage known as Hells Gates. From 1822 to 1833 its Sarah Island held one of the harshest penal stations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, for convicts who had reoffended in the colony. The town of Strahan on its shore later served the mining district around Queenstown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/macquarie-harbour.jpg" alt="Macquarie Harbour" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M. Murphy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MacquarieHarbour.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
